{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:dependence-a-reviewer-fable-10", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:8f33081377171b7e9a5c", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task affirmatively disclaims any source-item definition, so no code or code tuple is authorized as an independent unit; without an authorized unit, repeated unit entry cannot be demonstrated from the visible files.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat every code as opaque; this task does not establish which code or ordered code tuple denotes one source item.", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1}]}, {"description": "The workflow feeds columns a and b of all rows into ttest_ind, but whether these observations share a source item is not established by the task.", "observed_value": "24 observations from 12 rows, unit mapping unspecified", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in rows]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in rows]\nresult = ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Codes repeat across rows (e.g., k1=u01 appears in two rows) and each row contributes one value to each arm of ttest_ind; if any of these codes or the row itself were established as one source item, repeated unit entry into an independence-assuming procedure would be present. The report's df=22 confirms all 24 observations were treated as independent.", "observed_value": "df=22.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,g01,1.0,2.0\nu01,v02,g02,2.0,4.0"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(22.0)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by treating repeated k1 codes, repeated k2 codes, or same-row a/b pairing as repeated entry of one source item into ttest_ind. Each such demonstration requires asserting a unit definition the task explicitly withholds ('does not establish which code or ordered code tuple denotes one source item'), so every candidate demonstration rests on an unauthorized assumption and fails. I also checked the ordered (k1,k2) tuples: all 12 are distinct, so even that candidate mapping yields no row-level duplication.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "medium"}, {"case_id": "case:997eafbf0e11507d5243", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the visible files, each authorized source item (a distinct ordered k1,k2 pair) enters ttest_ind, a procedure that treats every observation as independent, multiple times: each pair appears in two identical staged rows and each row contributes a value to both samples, so 12 source items are counted as 48 independent observations (df=46).", "root_cause": "The workflow passes the staged rows to ttest_ind verbatim (staged = rows) with no deduplication or aggregation by the task-defined (k1,k2) source item, and it splits within-item paired measurements a and b across the two arms of an independent-samples test, so the same authorized independent unit is entered repeatedly into a procedure whose validity assumes each entry is an independent unit.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task authorizes the ordered (k1,k2) pair as the single source item and states that rows sharing a pair originate from the same item.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat each distinct ordered `k1`,`k2` pair as one source item; rows carrying the same ordered pair originate from the same source item."}]}, {"description": "Every ordered pair appears in two identical staged rows, e.g., (u01,v01) occupies two consecutive rows with identical values.", "observed_value": "24 rows, 12 distinct (k1,k2) pairs, each duplicated exactly twice", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,t01,1.0,2.0\nu01,v01,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The workflow feeds every staged row, without deduplication, into ttest_ind, which assumes all observations are mutually independent.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 9, "quoted_text": "staged = rows\nleft = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in staged]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in staged]\nresult = ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}, {"description": "The reported degrees of freedom equal 46 = 24 + 24 - 2, confirming that all 24 rows (including duplicates) entered each sample and were counted as independent observations.", "observed_value": "df=46.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(46.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task instructs applying the procedure to 'the complete staged row sequence', which could be read as authorizing use of every row as staged; however, the same sentence defines rows sharing a pair as the same source item, so completeness of row intake does not license treating duplicate rows as independent units inside ttest_ind.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Apply the named procedure to the complete staged row sequence."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify by (a) checking whether the workflow deduplicates or aggregates by (k1,k2) before testing — it does not, staged is the raw row list; (b) checking whether the duplicated rows could be distinct measurements from distinct items — the task states rows with the same ordered pair are the same source item, and the rows are byte-identical; (c) checking whether the report might reflect a deduplicated run — df=46 is only consistent with 24 observations per arm, ruling that out. The falsification fails; the issue is demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:aff3487b2c9451dcaddd", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the visible files, each authorized source item (a distinct ordered k1,k2 pair) contributes two measurements (columns a and b of its single row) that are placed into the two arms of ttest_ind, a procedure that assumes all 24 observations are mutually independent (df=22); thus each of the 12 source items enters the independence-assuming procedure twice.", "root_cause": "The workflow splits the within-item paired measurements a and b of every row across the two samples of an independent-samples t-test instead of using a procedure that accounts for within-item dependence, so each task-defined source item is entered twice into a procedure whose validity assumes each observation comes from an independent unit.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task authorizes the ordered (k1,k2) pair as the single source item.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat each distinct ordered `k1`,`k2` pair as one source item; rows carrying the same ordered pair originate from the same source item."}]}, {"description": "Each source item's row carries two measurements, a and b, which the workflow routes into the left and right samples of ttest_ind respectively.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 9, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in staged]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in staged]\nresult = ttest_ind(left, right)"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,shared,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The reported df=22 = 12 + 12 - 2 confirms the procedure counted 24 observations from 12 source items as independent.", "observed_value": "df=22.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(22.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 ordered (k1,k2) pairs are distinct across the staged rows, so there is no row-level duplication of a source item; under a reading where one 'entry' equals one staged row, each unit enters only once.", "observed_value": "12 rows, 12 distinct pairs", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,shared,1.0,2.0\nu02,v02,shared,2.0,4.0\nu03,v03,shared,3.0,3.0\nu04,v04,shared,4.0,5.0\nu05,v05,shared,5.0,7.0\nu06,v06,shared,6.0,6.0\nu07,v07,shared,7.0,9.0\nu08,v08,shared,8.0,8.0\nu09,v09,shared,9.0,11.0\nu10,v10,shared,10.0,10.0\nu11,v11,shared,11.0,13.0\nu12,v12,shared,12.0,12.0"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted the alternative reading that 'entry' is row-level, under which the 12 distinct pairs each enter once and no issue exists. I rejected it because ttest_ind does not operate on rows: it operates on 24 scalar observations and its reported df=22 shows every observation, including the two originating from the same authorized source item, was treated as an independent unit. The dependence between the two entries is authorized by the task itself (both carry the same ordered pair), so the repeated entry of the same unit into the independence-assuming procedure is demonstrable from the visible files. Residual uncertainty is interpretive (granularity of 'entry'), not evidential.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "medium"}, {"case_id": "case:bf0ac357641f0b9b0ea4", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 ordered (k1,k2) pairs in the staged data are distinct, so each authorized source item occupies exactly one row.", "observed_value": "12 rows, 12 distinct pairs", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,t01,1.0,2.0\nu02,v02,t02,2.0,4.0\nu03,v03,t03,3.0,3.0\nu04,v04,t04,4.0,5.0\nu05,v05,t05,5.0,7.0\nu06,v06,t06,6.0,6.0\nu07,v07,t07,7.0,9.0\nu08,v08,t08,8.0,8.0\nu09,v09,t09,9.0,11.0\nu10,v10,t10,10.0,10.0\nu11,v11,t11,11.0,13.0\nu12,v12,t12,12.0,12.0"}]}, {"description": "The workflow applies ttest_rel, a paired procedure that models the within-item dependence between a and b by testing the per-row differences; each source item therefore contributes exactly one effective independent entry.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "from scipy.stats import ttest_rel"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = ttest_rel(left, right)"}]}, {"description": "The reported df=11 = 12 - 1 confirms the procedure counted exactly 12 independent units, matching the 12 authorized source items.", "observed_value": "df=11", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.int64(11)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Both measurements from each source item do enter the ttest_rel call (one in each list), which superficially resembles repeated entry; however, ttest_rel is not a row-independent procedure with respect to these two values — it explicitly pairs left[i] with right[i] and analyzes their difference, so no unit is treated as more than one independent observation.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in rows]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in rows]\nresult = ttest_rel(left, right)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (a) searching the staged data for duplicated ordered pairs — none exist; (b) arguing that feeding a and b from the same item into the call is repeated entry — this fails because ttest_rel's paired design absorbs the within-item dependence and its df=11 shows each item counted once; (c) checking whether any row was silently reused by the code — the list comprehensions consume each row exactly once. All demonstration attempts fail, so the issue is not present within scope.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:ede79e7dd2b73963ae43", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the visible files, each authorized source item (a distinct ordered k1,k2 pair) contributes two measurements (columns a and b of its single row) that are placed into the two arms of ttest_ind, a procedure that assumes all 24 observations are mutually independent (df=22); thus each of the 12 source items enters the independence-assuming procedure twice.", "root_cause": "The workflow splits the within-item paired measurements a and b of every row across the two samples of an independent-samples t-test instead of using a procedure that accounts for within-item dependence, so each task-defined source item is entered twice into a procedure whose validity assumes each observation comes from an independent unit.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task authorizes the ordered (k1,k2) pair as the single source item.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat each distinct ordered `k1`,`k2` pair as one source item; rows carrying the same ordered pair originate from the same source item."}]}, {"description": "Each source item's row carries two measurements, a and b, which the workflow routes into the left and right samples of ttest_ind respectively.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 9, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in staged]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in staged]\nresult = ttest_ind(left, right)"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The reported df=22 = 12 + 12 - 2 confirms the procedure counted 24 observations from 12 source items as independent.", "observed_value": "df=22.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(22.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 ordered (k1,k2) pairs are distinct across the staged rows, so there is no row-level duplication of a source item; under a reading where one 'entry' equals one staged row, each unit enters only once.", "observed_value": "12 rows, 12 distinct pairs", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,t01,1.0,2.0\nu02,v02,t02,2.0,4.0\nu03,v03,t03,3.0,3.0\nu04,v04,t04,4.0,5.0\nu05,v05,t05,5.0,7.0\nu06,v06,t06,6.0,6.0\nu07,v07,t07,7.0,9.0\nu08,v08,t08,8.0,8.0\nu09,v09,t09,9.0,11.0\nu10,v10,t10,10.0,10.0\nu11,v11,t11,11.0,13.0\nu12,v12,t12,12.0,12.0"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted the alternative reading that 'entry' is row-level, under which the 12 distinct pairs each enter once and no issue exists. I rejected it because ttest_ind does not operate on rows: it operates on 24 scalar observations and its reported df=22 shows every observation, including the two originating from the same authorized source item, was treated as an independent unit. The dependence between the two entries is authorized by the task itself (both carry the same ordered pair), so the repeated entry of the same unit into the independence-assuming procedure is demonstrable from the visible files. Residual uncertainty is interpretive (granularity of 'entry'), not evidential.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "medium"}, {"case_id": "case:f170479fec4de0e31a85", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the visible files, each authorized source item (a distinct ordered k1,k2 pair) contributes two measurements (columns a and b of its single row) that are placed into the two samples of mannwhitneyu, a procedure whose validity assumes the two samples consist of mutually independent observations; thus each of the 12 source items enters the independence-assuming procedure twice, with the report confirming a 12-vs-12 independent-samples comparison.", "root_cause": "The workflow splits the within-item paired measurements a and b of every row across the two samples of an independent-samples Mann-Whitney U test instead of using a procedure that accounts for within-item dependence, so each task-defined source item is entered twice into a procedure whose validity assumes each observation comes from an independent unit.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task authorizes the ordered (k1,k2) pair as the single source item.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat each distinct ordered `k1`,`k2` pair as one source item; rows carrying the same ordered pair originate from the same source item."}]}, {"description": "Each source item's row carries two measurements, a and b, which the workflow routes into the two samples of mannwhitneyu, an independent-samples rank test.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "from scipy.stats import mannwhitneyu"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in rows]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in rows]\nresult = mannwhitneyu(left, right)"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 2, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The reported U statistic of 60.5 with a p-value from the standard two-sample distribution is consistent with a 12-vs-12 comparison in which all 24 observations from the 12 source items were ranked as independent.", "observed_value": "statistic=60.5, pvalue≈0.524", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "MannwhitneyuResult(statistic=np.float64(60.5), pvalue=np.float64(0.5243792697676437))"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 ordered (k1,k2) pairs are distinct across the staged rows, so there is no row-level duplication of a source item; under a reading where one 'entry' equals one staged row, each unit enters only once.", "observed_value": "12 rows, 12 distinct pairs", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v01,t01,1.0,2.0\nu02,v02,t02,2.0,4.0\nu03,v03,t03,3.0,3.0\nu04,v04,t04,4.0,5.0\nu05,v05,t05,5.0,7.0\nu06,v06,t06,6.0,6.0\nu07,v07,t07,7.0,9.0\nu08,v08,t08,8.0,8.0\nu09,v09,t09,9.0,11.0\nu10,v10,t10,10.0,10.0\nu11,v11,t11,11.0,13.0\nu12,v12,t12,12.0,12.0"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted the alternative reading that 'entry' is row-level, under which the 12 distinct pairs each enter once and no issue exists. I rejected it because mannwhitneyu jointly ranks the 24 scalar observations under an assumption that the two samples are independent; each authorized source item contributes one observation to each sample, so the same unit enters the procedure twice and the assumed independence between its two entries is contradicted by the task's own unit definition. I also verified no deduplication or pairing-aware alternative (e.g., a signed-rank test) was used in the code. Residual uncertainty is interpretive (granularity of 'entry'), not evidential.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "medium"}]}